Z||000000||GTMike||07-18-2001||11:48 PM||||so my car  87 gt.   just started ideling hight today.   i get code 24 and 35.   whats this mean.  please help.   <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||07-18-2001||11:54 PM||||You likely have a bad/cracked EGR yube.   Code 35 is the IAC (idle air control) and 24 is the speed sensor.<P>With the engine idling spray some WD-40 at the ends of the tube (where it meets the plenum and EGR valve), if the idle changes at all (either up or down) you have a crack.<P>They are fairly easy to change and will cost you about $75 or so.<P>If you want to drive it down to Brighton this weekend I could look it over for you/fix the problems......I might even have a good used EGR tube.  LMK.<P>   ||||reg||1
Z||000002||GTMike||07-19-2001||12:08 AM||||well i'm out there looking around  i went to go get a shop manual but b&n dont have one so i'm going to try to parts store tomarrow. <P>it has been ideling and running perfect and then just all of a sudded started ideling high.   <P>i think i tested the egr   is it the thing it the rear driverside of the eng.  and looks like it goes in the exauset.  and if you push your finger up on the diaphram from under it is makes the car stumble.  i tested that a few days  ago just for the heck of it. <P>i disconnected the battary   to reset the computher   i dont know how old the codes are.  does it erase the codes  after you disconnect the battery?   <P>i'll talk it for a drive after and see what the codes are.<BR>thanks||||reg||1
Z||000003||GTMike||07-19-2001||12:20 AM||||ok reset computer took her around the block and only got a code 24.  i'm going to take her for a longer ride here in a min and see if i get anything else.   also i though code 32s were egr<P>ok took it for another spinn and  only a code 24 pops up. <BR>[This message has been edited by GTMike (edited 07-19-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by GTMike (edited 07-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfiero||07-19-2001||12:54 AM||||Code 32 is the EGR.....this is usually just a vacuum leak and won't cause a high idle.  Code 35 is the IAC.......when you have a severe vacuum leak the idle shoots up and trips the IAC code.  Rarely, if ever, is the IAC valve the culprit.  It is usually the EGR tube that is broken, causing a huge vacuum leak and subsequently a code 35.<P>Code 24 is a puzzler.....is this an auto. or 5-sp.?  I had an auto. GT trip code 24 in conjunction with the code 35......I fixed the EGR tube, but the 24 stayed.  I never did figure it out.....I sold the car before I could!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>Code 35 should trip whenever the idle stays above the recommended value for a period of time, so it won't necessarily trip while driving.......just when it is supposed to be idling.<P>BTW......unplugging the battery will clear the codes, so any new codes that are set afterwards are issues that need to be looked into.<P>Good luck.||||reg||1
