Z||000006||GTMike||07-19-2001||03:26 AM||||ok well i did a search  and read a ton of high idle  posts.  and every oen says its the egr.   well i tested mine by pushing up on the diaphram  and it does   make the engine stumble.  so dose that mean i can rule out the egr and the tube?||||reg||1
Z||000007||GTMike||07-19-2001||03:58 AM||||ok so this has been pretty much a conversation with myself  but hey i guess thats what you get when you work on your car at 2am.  well  i'm happy to say i found the problem and all of you were right. its the egr tube.   i was out there in my pjs(boxers) and a flash light.     started her up. and then went a wigglein things around.  got the egr tube and pulled down towards the eng.  and vaaroomm up go the rpms.  humm... push up and to the right  shes purring like a kitten. so now all i have to do is get one of these tubes. <P>thanks every body. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||terryk||07-19-2001||12:56 PM||||Code 24 is the VSS. Since the VSS drives the speedo them to the ECM, the speedo will work but the ECM may not be seeing pulses.||||reg||1
Z||000009||mrfiero||07-19-2001||08:00 PM||||Pushing up on the EGR valve diaphram   won't tell you if the EGR tube is cracked.  Try the WD-40 test.  The tube has either a tinfoil covered cloth covering or a metal shrouding as a heat shield.  It attaches to the base of teh EGR valve and the underside of the plenum.<P><BR>Code 24 is a weird one......like I said, I had a GT do this to me and I never did find out what the problem was.  It was an auto. and I swapped teh VSS with a known good one (from my 16K mile GT), but it stil l set the code.  It could be a bad wire somewhere or a bad ECM.<P> <P>||||reg||1
